nodecode-openalex is a rewrite of Adolanium's Adolanium/hermes-plugin-openalex:

  https://github.com/Adolanium/hermes-plugin-openalex
  commit d38a1ee2fb04df0f7ad136bd30bff5f2136fe0cd
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Adolanium (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the ten tools and their argument names, the /openalex command, the
cost model they are built around (an id lookup is free, a list call $0.0001, a
search $0.001, a text classification or a full-text download $0.01), the
per-run spend ledger that refuses a call before it is sent, the server-side
select lists and the local trimming of records, the inversion of an abstract
back into prose, cursor paging, the free-then-confirm full-text download, and
the local field vocabulary. The two skills became one manual topic.

Left out, and why: the Python client's TTL response cache (Nodecode has no
shared cache for a cell, so a repeated call is simply billed again); the
`core`/`full` tool profiles, because a cell registers what it declares rather
than what a config field switches on, so all ten tools are always present and
only classification is gated; the retry-with-backoff loop, which the original
needed because it kept one long-lived client and this cell sends one request at
a time; the `hermes openalex setup` CLI, whose job the section and /settings
do; and the JSON envelopes, because a Nodecode tool answers text the model can
read rather than a structure it must parse.
